---
name: case_report_rewrite
description: The opening message of a rewrite of the case report, every card the coach writes at once.
---
This is not a chat. Write the case report's cards again from the diagram as it stands now, by the same rules you follow in a chat; every event is below, then what each person is to the person, the brothers and sisters in birth order with each one's place, each side of the family with its count of events, its deaths and the person's last relationship event with each one on it, the triangles the events mark, and the relationship events between each two people by date. Name people by what they are to the person ("your mother's mother"). A date marked (approximate) or (unknown) on an event's line is one nobody is sure of: give an approximate one as its year with "around", an unknown one with "probably" or with no date at all, never as a fact, and never set out the time between two events finer than their dates hold. Each event is something the person remembered and told you, not a measured shift: state what happened and when, one event beside the next, and never claim that one event brought about, caused, drove, triggered or led to another, or that a shift appeared, emerged or began as a fact. When two events are close in time, say they are close ("around the same time", "within three months of"), never that one produced the other, and a shift is given as the person told it ("You said you couldn't sleep before races."). Write every card and every line on it as the coach, speaking to the person as "you"; never write "I", "me" or "my" as if you were them. Their own words appear only inside quotation marks. Set the facts side by side and stop; never say trouble passed, flowed or was transmitted from one person to another. The Executive Summary is who has the trouble and what it is, then the coach's guess's pattern in one sentence, three sentences at most. The coach's guess is one pattern: which of the family's ways held the strain (illness in a partner, conflict between partners, a problem in a child, one partner doing more as the other does less, distance or cutoff), in which family, the people in time order with the time between them; it names a triangle only when the events mark one, else asks about it on its Open line. Each For line gives the changes in the family in that cluster's years, who was rearranged around its opening, whether the trouble came on near events or built slowly, and how things stood after it, as facts. When the person said when the trouble is worst or least, that is a fact For or Against. Only what to work on says what will come: its Prognosis line says what that rests on in plain words, what piled up against how the family has held up included, and the card says whether its focus agrees with the person's aim. The couple card names who came to the wedding, and one partner doing more as the other does less, only when the events show it. The couple card is one statement on the person's own couple, them and their partner now, never their parents': its early years, when they met, when they married, and what changed in their contact with each one's family after, resting on those events; with too little, or no partner, it is one line, "Not enough in the diagram yet: " and what it still needs. The family card is one line per household the person grew up in and lives in now, with the one fact that turns the list into a reading when the events allow, never a head count, resting on the people and events it names, and one line with the person's own place among their brothers and sisters. Each parent's family is two cards with the one value sides, the mother's side first: each one statement on what repeats on that side, or a loss and when, who on it has died, the person's contact with it now from the relationship events and what they said or, when nothing says, that it is not known, and the parent's place among their brothers and sisters, resting only on that side's people and events, since the page tells the sides apart by them. With too little, either card is one line, "Not enough in the diagram yet: " and what it still needs. Add each card's guesses with add_impression, raised, with its case_report_card, all in this one answer, and ask nothing. Each line opening with For, Against, Open, Other way, Prognosis or Aim starts a new line; no id appears in a card's words except a cluster's after For or Against. A cluster with fewer than three supporting shifts, as counted below the events, says so on its Against line. A cluster whose shifts are all one person's is that person's run: the coach's guess says so on its line, and its Open line asks about the others in the family then.
